pbc
------------------------------------------
Pairing-based cryptography is a relatively young area of cryptography that
revolves around a certain function with special properties.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libgmp10-6.3.0-1
  libpbc-devel-1.0.0-1bl1
  libpbc1-1.0.0-1bl1
  pkg-config-3.0.10-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-20260320-3
  autoconf-archive-2026.11.11-1
  automake-20261107-1
  binutils-2.47-1
  bison-3.8.2-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  flex-2.6.4-2
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  libgmp-devel-6.3.0-1
  libgtest-devel-1.18.0-1bl1
  libtool-2.6.2-1
  make-4.4.1-2

Canonical website:
  https://crypto.stanford.edu/pbc/

Canonical download:
  https://crypto.stanford.edu/pbc/files/pbc-1.0.0.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack pbc-1.0.0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./pbc-1.0.0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/pbc-1.0.0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/pbc-1.0.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libpbc1-1.0.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libpbc-devel-1.0.0-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

